## Solo Reactivation Check (T4+)

**When:** Runs inside the nightly workflow (T4)
**Wall-clock:** < 1 minute
**Gating:** Hard failure — blocks the nightly run and alerts via workflow failure

The reactivation check (`scripts/check-solo-reactivation.mjs`) detects when the
project's team composition has grown beyond the single-developer threshold:

| Condition | Threshold | Action |
|-----------|-----------|--------|
| Distinct active authors (30d) | ≥ 3 | Exit 1, print remediation |
| `EXTERNAL_AUDIT=true` env var | any value | Exit 1, print remediation |

**Remediation when triggered:**

1. Update `arbiter.json`: `collaborationMode` → `"peer-review"` or `"gated-review"`
2. Add `CODEOWNERS` file with required reviewers
3. Enable branch protection: `required_approving_review_count: 1`
4. Re-run `node arbiter update` to regenerate CI with full review gates

This check is the technical enforcement of the reactivation trigger declared in
`docs/governance/SOLO_DEV_EXCEPTION.md`.

<% } %>

